# Chat — the durable message model (threads, reactions, read state)

The Studio chat lane is ordinary `resource` rows, so messages ride the same tenant partitioning,
live-shapes deltas (`Nexus.Shapes`), and keyset pagination as everything else in the store. The
threading model is **one field** — `parent` — declared from the start so threads are never a painful
retrofit onto a flat table (wb-d8ac.4). Reactions and read cursors are their own tiny shapes
(wb-d8ac.5, wb-d8ac.3). The view logic — assembling threads, aggregating reactions, computing unread
and @-mention badges authoritatively on the server — is `Nexus.Chat` (generic, not our opinion).

resource Message do
  description "A chat message in a channel. parent='' is top-level; else it is a threaded reply."
  tags ["chat", "event"]
  channel :string   # which channel/surface this message belongs to
  author :string    # user id who wrote it
  body :string      # the message text
  parent :string    # "" = top-level; otherwise the id of the message this replies to (THREADS)
  ts :integer       # unix milliseconds — the order key
end

resource Reaction do
  description "An emoji reaction on a message. One row per (message, emoji, author)."
  tags ["chat"]
  message :string   # the message id reacted to
  emoji :string     # the reaction glyph
  author :string    # who reacted
  ts :integer       # unix milliseconds
end

resource Cursor do
  description "A per-user read cursor: how far a user has read in a channel (drives unread badges)."
  tags ["chat"]
  channel :string   # the channel
  user :string      # whose read state this is
  ts :integer       # the ts of the last message they have read
end
